  "grading_output": "**REASONING**: The candidate diagnosis exactly matches the reference in core disease, immunophenotypic subtype, anatomic involvement, and associated complication.\n\nThe reported deep skin-biopsy results confirm intravascular large B-cell lymphoma: large atypical CD20-positive/PAX5-positive B cells occupy small-vessel lumina delineated by CD31/CD34-positive endothelium, with a Ki-67 index of approximately 95%. MUM1 positivity, CD10 negativity, and weak BCL6 expression support the non–germinal-center immunophenotype. Marrow re-review also confirms intrasinusoidal lymphoma involvement.\n\nCutaneous involvement is established histologically and corresponds to the livedoid and telangiectatic lesions. CNS involvement is supported by progressive encephalopathy and multifocal cerebral infarcts of differing ages without a large-vessel or cardiac embolic source. Negative CSF cytology does not exclude this predominantly intravascular disease.\n\nThe associated secondary hemophagocytic lymphohistiocytosis is supported by fever, splenomegaly, hypertriglyceridemia, elevated ferritin and soluble IL-2 receptor, and marrow hemophagocytosis, with lymphoma identified as the underlying trigger.\n\nThere are no omitted reference components, incorrect qualifiers, or unrelated added diagnoses.\n\n**SCORE**: 5",
